    "unit": 11,
    "title": "Relative Clauses (who/which/that)",
    "title_ko": "관계대명사 (who/which/that)",
    "focus_axis": "grammar"
  },
  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "Relative clauses add information about a noun without starting a new sentence. Use 'who' for people, 'which' for things, and 'that' for either: 'The man who called is my boss.' 'The book that/which I read was great.'",
    "explanation_ko": "관계대명사절은 새 문장을 시작하지 않고 명사에 대한 정보를 추가합니다. 사람에는 'who', 사물에는 'which', 둘 다에는 'that'을 씁니다: 'The man who called is my boss.' 'The book that/which I read was great.'",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "The person who helped me was very kind.",
        "ko": "저를 도와준 사람은 아주 친절했어요."
      },
      {
        "en": "This is the phone that I bought last week.",
        "ko": "이게 지난주에 산 휴대폰이에요."
      },
      {
        "en": "The movie which we watched was boring.",
        "ko": "우리가 본 영화는 지루했어요."
      }
    ]
  },
